 "verdict": {
  "hall": "ELIMINATED. \u03b4 = 1.597e-07 reproduces Mercury but predicts Venus 16.8\u2033 (measured 8.62), Earth 10.4\u2033 (3.84), Mars 5.5\u2033 (1.35) and a lunar perigee excess of 1.38\u2033/yr against an LLR limit of ~1e-4\u2033/yr.",
  "ring": "ELIMINATED. An exterior ring at 1 AU would need 0.61 M\u2295 (4e+07\u00d7 the zodiacal cloud); at 0.6 AU 0.13 M\u2295. Interior dust regresses, not advances. The asteroid belt's real contribution is 0.0014\u2033/cy.",
  "masses": "ELIMINATED. Budget reproduced (total 553.2\u2033/cy vs classical 531). Venus would need a 15.0 % mass error against 1e-9 relative (\u00d72e+08); Jupiter 26.8 % against 1e-8 (\u00d73e+07).",
  "row_10": "No Newtonian cause of Mercury's 43\u2033/century survives measurement: solar J2 (report \u00a7), inner planet/ring (report \u00a7), Hall's exponent, exterior zodiacal mass, and perturbing-mass error are each excluded by more than two orders of magnitude. The residual stands as an unexplained measurement under the rules of this audit. This statement is a receipt; it is also an arrow, recorded and not followed (see GAMEPLAN \u00a73, REFLECTION \u00a72)."
